    "<strong>1.</strong> Four or five paragraphs, and the <strong>position</strong> (opinion) in paragraph one. <br><strong>2.</strong> The position again at the end, in new words. No new idea. <br><strong>3.</strong> Every part of the question is answered. <br><strong>4.</strong> Each body: one idea, a <strong>mechanism</strong> (how it works), an example. <br><strong>5.</strong> Each body has a <strong>nuance</strong> (a limit). The position stays. <br><strong>6.</strong> No linker on every sentence. <br><strong>7.</strong> No memorised phrases. No <em>research shows</em>. <br><strong>8.</strong> <strong>Register</strong> (formal style). No contractions (<em>don't</em>), no <em>you</em>, no questions, no bullet points. <br><strong>9.</strong> Only grammar you control. <br><strong>10.</strong> 260 to 290 words.",
